WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.270
Mifune

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.270
Touto

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.270
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Suzuki-kun.</i>

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:06.400
Just don't give up a homer.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.150
If we get these next 
two out, victory is ours.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.620
Okay!

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:13.900
Strike!

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.160
Touto Boys

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.160
Pitcher  Mayumura Michiru

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.410
Catcher

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.410
Suzuki Andy

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.410
<i>They're even more impressive up close.</i>

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:25.370
Oh, right. Those pitches are one thing for 
a right-hander, but for a lefty like Andy...

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:29.250
Mifune Dolphins

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:29.250
Coach  Fujii

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:29.250
Mifune Dolphins

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:29.250
Manager  Tashiro

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:29.710
Yeah. He probably feels like the pitches
are coming from behind him.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:32.880
Strike two!

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.140
Touto Boys

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.140
Catcher  Mayumura Wataru

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.640
<i>Good! We've got them now.</i>

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.150
<i>That second run we conceded in the fifth</i>

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.770
<i>was my fault because I wasn't 
watching for the squeeze play.</i>

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:46.400
<i>I made the mistake. Now, I have 
to make up for it with my bat!</i>

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.100
Foul!

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.550
Good job!

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.690
Second base

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.690
Katsumata

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.690
First base

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.690
Matsubara

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:50.690
Go!

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.940
Pitcher

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.940
Urabe Hayato

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.940
Hit it, Andy!

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:56.030
<i>I joined the Dolphins to 
defeat the Touto Boys.</i>

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.660
<i>Our entire team has pulled 
together to create this chance.</i>

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.540
<i>If I don't live up to 
everyone's expectations here,</i>

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.710
<i>I can't call myself a cleanup hitter!</i>

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.250
Wh-What?!

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.320
Yes!

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.630
Awesome!

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.980
Stop, stop!

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.160
All right!

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.680
Touto Boys

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.680
Manager  Inui

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.480
Bases... loaded?

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.940
Center field

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.940
Satou Hikaru

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.940
<i>Batting fifth, center field, Satou-kun.</i>

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:16.880
The Hit of Destiny

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.010
One out, bases loaded, huh?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.480
They're doing amazingly well!

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.270
If Hikaru-kun hits a home run here,
it'll be one hell of a comeback story!

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:35.730
Time out!

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.070
Their manager's making a move.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.560
You're getting over-excited, Michiru.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.060
That was their cleanup.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.930
Instead of just hitting the corners,
you should've drawn it out.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:51.910
Y-Yes, sir.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.340
We're going to walk Satou.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.830
W-Walk him?

00:03:58.830 --> 00:03:59.990
But the bases are loaded!

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:01.300
That'll give them a run!

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.070
They're welcome to it.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:06.300
It's less risky than taking on Satou.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.450
Taking on the two hitters
after him is a lot safer.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.480
Walk him.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.080
Am I clear?

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:14.900
Understood.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.910
Right field

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.910
Sakura Mutsuko

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.770
Play!

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:43.050
Are you serious?!

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:45.900
<i>They're going to walk him 
with the bases loaded?</i>

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.320
Ball!

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.510
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:59.570
<i>No one in the bottom of our lineup 
has a hope of hitting her pitches.</i>

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.140
Ball two.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:09.950
Time out.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.510
You seem unhappy, Michiru.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.170
Aren't you on board with this strategy?

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:27.970
I-It's fine.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.650
Be honest.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:33.090
Do you want to win by getting Satou out?

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.860
Yes. I want to win by facing them head on.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:43.780
I don't think a team that uses a tactic 
like this to avoid a fight in Regionals

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:47.700
has <i>any</i> hope of making it to the very top!

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:49.450
Michiru...

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:57.090
And don't you always say that junior 
baseball isn't just about winning, Manager?

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:03.110
It's about being proud of yourself for 
being better than you were yesterday!

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:04.960
Please let me take him on!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.680
I want to keep playing with my head held high!

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.510
I <i>promise</i> I'll get him out!

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.060
All right.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.020
I'll allow it.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.160
Well? How do you plan on getting him out?

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.860
I have an idea.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:30.480
Leave it to me.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:38.680
He's squatting!

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:39.770
They're ready to fight!

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.160
<i>Bring it on, Michiru.</i>

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:45.350
<i>I'm surprised.</i>

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:48.940
<i>I didn't think she had it in her to 
challenge the manager and her catcher.</i>

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.750
<i>But that's why... she's our ace!</i>

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.640
Strike!

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.670
<i>I won't let you hit.</i>

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:02.390
<i>I'm going to take you down with 
the pitch I've admired for so long.</i>

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:03.530
<i>I swear it!</i>

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:08.760
<i>Back in third grade,</i>

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:13.120
<i>I didn't know much about baseball yet,
 and I had no real interest in it.</i>

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:18.190
<i>I knew my father was a pro,
but he was retired by then.</i>

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.620
<i>Two of my three older siblings 
didn't care about baseball, either.</i>

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.860
<i>Then, one day, Wataru, whose interest 
in baseball was starting to grow big time,</i>

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:28.170
<i>sat and watched one of Dad's old videos.</i>

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:31.630
<i>It was the one where Dad was
playing in the World Series,</i>

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.640
<i>back before we were born.</i>

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:38.490
<i>That was the first time I saw </i>him<i>...</i>

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:44.450
<i>Ever since that day, the pitching 
style I've adored the most...</i>

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:53.200
<i>...is the left-handed overhead 
Shigeno Goro throws!</i>

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.120
Strike!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.450
What was <i>that</i>?!

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.830
All this time, she's had an 
overhead throw up her sleeve?

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:14.050
And it's her fastest pitch yet!

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:20.360
<i>She... She's been practicing 
an overhead throw in secret?</i>

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:26.010
<i>A year ago, I started getting 
a pain in my elbow when pitching.</i>

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:29.180
<i>My dad banned me from pitching 
 till I reach middle school.</i>

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:31.290
<i>That's when I started catching.</i>

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:38.890
<i>Manager made Michiru a pitcher,
and she started off pitching overhead,</i>

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:42.290
<i>but she couldn't control it, 
so she switched to the sidearm.</i>

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:47.050
<i>Since that worked out so well,</i>

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:50.230
<i>I thought she'd given up on the overhead...</i>

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:54.970
<i>But it looks like she never let go 
of her fascination with Shigeno Goro.</i>

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:00.490
Foul.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.850
<i>You won't be able to slug it now.</i>

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.100
<i>The third strike's coming up!</i>

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:10.470
We're counting on you, Hikaru!

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.320
I know you can hit 'em!

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:15.140
<i>Daigo-kun...</i>

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:17.860
<i>Okay!</i>

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.910
<i>You think he can hit these pitches?</i>

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:24.660
<i>Don't be stupid.</i>

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.900
<i>I've been saving this 
pitch for the Nationals,</i>

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.580
<i>and there's no </i>way<i> he can hit them!</i>

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:42.490
<i>No way...</i>

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:44.980
<i>This can't be happening.</i>

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:47.350
<i>Catch it.</i>

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:50.440
<i>You've got it, right?</i>

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:56.280
It made it!

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:57.360
<i>No way.</i>

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:00.660
6-8!

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.540
7-8!

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:07.580
<i>If I make it home, we're tied.</i>

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:15.600
Andy!

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.880
His leg!

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:22.810
Out!

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:24.860
Are you all right?

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:28.300
Andy!

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:29.850
Umpire!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:30.780
Pinch hitter: Nagai!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.310
Nagai

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.310
Third base

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.310
Ariyoshi

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:32.310
Who, me?!

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:37.570
M-Manager! The situation's 
totally different now!

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:40.320
We've closed the gap to one run,
 with a runner on second!

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:41.030
I'm not—

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.320
I told you I'd put you in if we got two outs.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:47.870
I don't want this game to be your last 
without you getting a chance to play.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:51.160
Look. Your parents came to cheer you on.

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:55.800
But I told them they didn't need to come 
because I was on the bench today.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:11:00.020
Even if they get you out, 
nobody will blame you.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.720
Pour your emotions of the last 
three years into that bat,

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.050
and swing without hesitation!

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.060
Y-Yes, sir!

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:07.770
Play!

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:11.080
Go get 'em!

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.260
Hit it, Nagai-kun!

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:15.260
Keep us rolling, Nagai!

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:17.570
If the game ends with you,
you'll have hell to pay!

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.420
<i>Of </i>course<i> I don't want the game to end.</i>

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.070
<i>But...</i>

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:26.450
Strike!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:32.460
<i>How am I even supposed 
to hit this devilish pitch?</i>

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:36.960
<i>It's insane.</i>

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.940
<i>How did he even </i>hit<i> that pitch?</i>

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:42.600
<i>I don't believe it!</i>

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:45.260
Strike two!

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:46.670
What is he swinging at?

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:48.560
Those were clearly balls!

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:52.940
<i>Michiru's really shook up
from Satou hitting her pitch.</i>

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:56.440
<i>Thank god this batter's an 
idiot who'll swing at anything.</i>

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.360
This is rough.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.170
Yeah.

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:02.950
Satou's just on another level. 
It's not like everyone can hit her pitches.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:06.440
Still, they ran Touto to the wire.

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:08.450
The kids have played great.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.960
<i>Damn. I really want to hit this ball!</i>

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.840
<i>For everyone's sake, I don't want it to be over.</i>

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:26.650
Run, Nagai!

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:34.020
It's a dropped third strike! Run!

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.520
<i>I won't let it end here!</i>

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:44.860
Safe, safe!

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.830
Komatsu! Back home!

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.040
Safe!

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.930
Hey, that's some hustle.

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:58.590
Yeah! That was amazing!

00:12:58.590 --> 00:12:59.800
Yeah!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.030
We caught up!

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:02.550
Thank you.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:04.710
Nice swing and run, Nagai!

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:06.180
You did good.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:08.540
I'm sorry.

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:10.050
I shouldn't have missed that ball.

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:11.140
It was my error.

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:12.690
Stop.

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:15.460
I threw a wild pitch. I'm to blame.

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:16.900
I'm sorry.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.060
It's not over yet!

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:24.170
All they did was tie the game.

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:25.740
We'll see this out and grab a walk-off hit!

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.650
R-Right.

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:30.160
Hey, don't touch me there!

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.100
Your overhead throw was something else.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:34.660
I was genuinely surprised by it.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:42.210
Strike!

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:43.210
Batter out!

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:44.340
Mifune

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:44.340
Touto

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:45.340
Three outs! Change sides!

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:50.790
As we feared, Andy can't carry on.

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:52.720
Daigo, you're the catcher now.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:54.240
Y-Yes, sir.

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:55.890
Nagai, you're in left field.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:56.730
Yes, sir!

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:02.230
I'll vary the pitches myself.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:05.340
You just tell me whether 
to go inside or outside.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:06.330
Okay.

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:08.700
How are you holding out, though?

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:11.700
I can't start whining now 
when we just tied the game.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:14.610
There's no way we're letting 
them get a walk-off hit.

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.830
We'll take this into extra innings 
and beat them there!

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:18.540
Yeah!

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:23.300
<i>Bottom of the seventh, 
Touto Boys to bat.</i>

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:26.300
<i>Batting seventh, third base, Nakamura-kun.</i>

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:28.300
Play!

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:35.060
Ball.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:37.560
Strike!

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:39.310
Foul.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.520
Out!

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:46.430
Yes!

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:48.320
Nice play, Takahashi!

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:52.180
<i>Batting eighth, shortstop, Sakai-kun.</i>

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:57.790
Left field!

00:14:58.130 --> 00:14:59.040
Nagai!

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:05.210
Out!

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:06.210
All right!

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:07.480
Nice one, Nagai!

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:09.090
We've got two outs now.

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:12.880
Two good plays in a row.

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.650
Looks like we're heading for extra innings.

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:16.440
The real showdown will 
come in the next inning.

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:21.050
<i>Batting ninth, first base, Komatsu-kun.</i>

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.690
Mayumura Ken

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:23.240
Dad!

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:32.490
<i>Get this guy out,
and we head into extra innings.</i>

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:38.790
All right!

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.400
Nice one, Komatsu!

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:42.570
Time out!

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:44.480
Pinch runner for first base.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:48.980
<i>Batting first, pitcher, 
Mayumura Michiru-san.</i>

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:54.970
<i>We've got two outs, but we still have 
to make sure she doesn't rope this one.</i>

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:57.750
Be careful!

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.230
Walk her if you have to.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:02.730
<i>Just one more.</i>

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:11.620
Strike!

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.110
<i>I won't let you get a walk-off hit here!</i>

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:17.660
<i>Dad...</i>

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:22.480
<i>Before now, he's never turned up 
to a single one of our games.</i>

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:25.750
<i>But today, he's come to one
for the first time.</i>

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:38.010
Safe!

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.870
Nice one, Micchi!

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:40.810
Let's wrap this up!

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.560
This is our chance to end the game!

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:44.490
Two outs, runners on first and second.

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:45.380
This is bad...

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:47.560
Yeah. They could wrap this up in one hit.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:53.690
<i>Batting second, second base, Hirata-kun.</i>

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:54.320
Play!

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:56.820
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:00.990
Ball!

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:06.290
<i>I jammed my middle finger in that last play.</i>

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:10.590
Ball!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.010
Ball two.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.340
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:22.120
<i>We've all fought tooth and nail to get here.</i>

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:26.600
<i>And we only need one more 
out and we change sides.</i>

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:37.580
Hit by pitch!

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:41.080
Time out!

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:44.830
What? Your finger?

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:51.610
I'm sorry, but I'm done.

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:53.580
If I keep pitching, we'll lose for sure.

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:56.400
There's only one thing we can do now.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.700
Satou, come here!

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.050
We're putting you in to pitch!

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.270
What?

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:07.050
But Hikaru-kun's already 
been knocked around...

00:18:07.050 --> 00:18:09.560
They must really be desperate.

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:13.910
I'm counting on you.

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.480
It hurts, doesn't it?

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.120
But I'm amazed you offered to
leave the game yourself.

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:34.420
Let's let the rookies 
take it from here.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:37.920
<i>Damn, they switched him out.</i>

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:42.860
<i>It's true that we took Satou out
earlier in the game,</i>

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.350
<i>but that was mostly because he imploded.</i>

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:51.810
<i>If he's reset since then, 
we could easily go into extra innings.</i>

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:55.440
You sure about putting 
Satou on the mound again?

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:56.910
He already choked once,

00:18:56.910 --> 00:19:00.440
and now you're putting him up there 
with bases loaded, needing one last out?

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:01.620
I'm not sure.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:05.140
He's surprisingly calm, though.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.210
He might be able to save the game for us.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:11.210
<i>Batting third, center field, Yuge-kun.</i>

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:12.390
Play!

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:14.800
<i>Come on, Hikaru.</i>

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:17.340
<i>Let your confidence soar 
and throw a scorcher!</i>

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:25.630
Strike!

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:31.050
<i>The baton's with me now, Urabe-kun!</i>

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:35.330
<i>Satou's completely recovered.</i>

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:39.440
<i>No. If anything, he looks like he's 
pitching even better than he was before.</i>

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.770
<i>I will </i>definitely<i> get him out.</i>

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:51.200
<i>For Daigo-kun's sake, because 
he's shown me how fun baseball is.</i>

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:58.140
<i>And for those two, who are banking 
everything on this one game.</i>

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:04.340
<i>For everyone who's given 
everything to be here...</i>

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:08.810
<i>I'm going to give it all I have!</i>

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:12.780
Strike two!

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:13.850
All right!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.320
We're almost there!

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:20.370
Dude... He's pitching emergency relief,
after his arm hard already cooled down...

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.150
What a monster!

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:25.680
<i>So this is Satou Toshiya's son.</i>

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:29.770
<i>He's still rough around the edges, 
but he has a lot of potential.</i>

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:32.270
Just one more strike.

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:34.040
Go get 'em, Hikaru-kun!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.180
<i>Wow. Hikaru really is a 
concentrated ball of talent.</i>

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:43.240
<i>If we just get this guy out, 
we can still win this.</i>

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:48.970
<i>We've got him!</i>

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.310
<i>We're going into overtime!</i>

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:11.320
Safe!

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:12.450
That's game!

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:20.490
You're kidding...

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:21.960
Th-The game's over...

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:38.940
W-We lost.

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.270
I'm sorry, Hika—

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:52.410
Satou!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:53.450
What's wrong, Satou?!

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:55.120
Wait! Don't move him!

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.280
Call an ambulance.

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:58.120
Someone, call 911!

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:58.920
Okay!

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.870
<i>What just... happened back there?</i>

00:22:12.870 --> 00:22:16.020
<i>How... did this happen?</i>

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:26.570
<i>I couldn't... stop shaking.</i>

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:01.290
Hikaru!

00:24:01.950 --> 00:24:04.280
No... It's all my fault!

00:24:04.280 --> 00:24:07.300
Losing the game. 
Hikaru getting hurt like that.

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:08.620
It's all my fault!

00:24:09.340 --> 00:24:10.830
I have to go see him.

00:24:10.830 --> 00:24:13.510
I need to see Hikaru and apologize!

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:16.750
So I can face baseball again!

00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:18.940
So him and me can set out together again!

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
No way...!

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:21.630
Next time: "No way...!"

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:24.540
Run to the stage of your dreams!
